from mkchar import write
S="Source_Text chapter files"
write("Zato","Zato","1","3","3","Book 3 (chapter files); notes for Book 3","Thadwick_Mercer.md, Humphrey_Geller.md, ../05_Organisations/Cults_and_Orders.md",
 "The last silver-ranker of the Builder cult's local forces, who leads its survivors to the Vane Estate.",
 "- \"The last silver-ranker left in the Builder cult's local forces\", he leads the evacuation of their island stronghold and escapes with many of their people; none of his fellow silver-rankers survive (Book 3, Ch7 L88-89).\n- Recruits Thadwick: \"I see your true potential\" (Book 3, Ch46 L60).\n- Asks what to do with the bronze-rankers when the cult cannot convert them with clockwork cores (Book 3, Ch60 L37).\n- Humphrey faces him in the climax, throwing his dragon sword (Book 3, Ch68 L59-61).",
 "Zealous and desperate; he talks of the Builder's glory while his people die.")
write("Shako","Shako","2","6","6","Book 6 (chapter files)","Dawn.md, Jason_Asano.md, ../02_Cosmology_and_Powers/Great_Astral_Beings.md",
 "A diamond-rank servant of the Builder who kills Jason in Book 6.",
 "- Introduces himself: \"I am Shako. I am a servant of the Builder\" (Book 6, Ch17 L41); he can enter through a window opened by the transformation event so long as he leaves before it closes (Book 6, Ch17 L43).\n- A presence takes him over and his aura rises from diamond rank to transcendent when the Builder speaks through him (Book 6, Ch18 L79-84).\n- Dawn warns him that killing Jason violated the compact between the Builder, the Reaper and the World-Phoenix (Book 6, Ch18 L79).\n- The Church of Death's certification says Jason has died four times so far (Book 7, Ch17 L104); the Master Timeline counts Shako's killing as the fourth.",
 "Impatient and proud; he believes he is the one in control.")
write("Elizabeth","Elizabeth (vampire queen)","3","6","13","Books 6, 11 (chapter files)","Simon_McKean.md, ../05_Organisations/Earth_Powers.md",
 "The gold-rank leader of the vampires who take Europe.",
 "- \"Their leader was known only as Elizabeth. She was a gold-ranker, and extremely tired of people asking if she was Elizabeth Bathory\" (Book 11, Ch68 L1488).\n- Combat with the vampires \"began in earnest shortly after\" Jason left; Rufus thinks he \"made an impression on the vampire leader, Elizabeth\" (Book 11, Ch42 L38).\n- Mr North and Elizabeth team up to set up defensive rituals against Jason in Book 6 (Book 6, Ch45 L39).\n- Gerling is later her blood slave (notes, Books 12 and 13).",
 "Amused, patient and predatory.")
write("Simon_McKean","Simon McKean","3","13","13","Book 13 (chapter files)","Elizabeth.md, Farrah_Hurin.md, ../05_Organisations/Earth_Powers.md",
 "The head of the Earth researchers in the Network's grid workgroup, who becomes Jason's final enemy on Earth.",
 "- Farrah: \"He was the head of the Earth researchers, ranked only behind myself in the workgroup\" (Book 13, Ch970 L38).\n- Boris says Jason will face a man who has spent a decade preparing; \"battling you is not a means but an end in itself\" (Book 13, Ch1000 L104).\n- Named again at the Ascension's Gate briefing (Book 13, Ch1002 L40).",
 "Theory-obsessed and patient; he treats the fight as his life's work.")
write("Lenora_Coleman","Lenora Coleman","1","12","13","Books 12, 13 (chapter files)","Anna_Tilden.md, ../06_Places/Earth/Artefact_Site_One.md",
 "The bureaucrat who runs the dimensional artefact site in Australia.",
 "- Has worked at the dimensional artefact site for almost her entire adult life, recruited out of university and \"two years in a monitoring station\" (Book 12, Ch61 L16).\n- Anna says she will \"play this objectively\" (Book 12, Ch62 L28).\n- Her deputy Barry is mayor of the artefact city (Book 12, Ch61 L25); she is a core-user and not a fighter (Book 12, Ch61 L22).",
 "Overworked, dry and more perceptive than she looks.")
write("Itsuki_Tiwari","Itsuki Tiwari","1","5","13","Books 5, 13 (chapter files); notes for Book 5","Jason_Asano.md, ../05_Organisations/Earth_Powers.md",
 "A young Japanese essence user who idolises Jason and has a doom confluence.",
 "- Introduces himself with a respectful bow: \"My name is Tiwari Itsuki\" (Book 5, Ch38 L5).\n- His essences are dark, blood and omen, forming a doom confluence (Book 5, Ch38 L50).\n- In 2038 he serves as an affliction specialist protected by Nigel's nine-person unit (Book 13, Ch1007 L23).",
 "Earnest, flustered and keen to please.")
write("Marek_Nior_Vargas","Marek Nior Vargas","2","9","11","Books 9, 11 (chapter files)","Tera_Jun_Casta.md, Boris_Ket_Lundi.md, ../02_Cosmology_and_Powers/Astral_Kings_and_Messengers.md",
 "A messenger who leads the breach force over Yaresh's entertainment district and later a free messenger.",
 "- Leads the breach force at Yaresh (Book 9, Ch86 L16); absently blocks a gold adventurer's projectile with his wing (Book 9, Ch87 L31).\n- Held in Jason's astral realm, he talks with Payan Nior Roel (Book 9, Ch104 L3) and says that knowing messengers can survive without an astral king will be a revelation (Book 9, Ch103 L114).\n- Leads Jason's messenger prisoners and plans their uprising (Book 10, Ch42 L4).",
 "Proud, adaptable and honest once his certainties break.")
write("Tera_Jun_Casta","Tera Jun Casta","2","9","11","Books 9, 10 (chapter files)","Marek_Nior_Vargas.md, Jason_Asano.md, ../02_Cosmology_and_Powers/Astral_Kings_and_Messengers.md",
 "A branded messenger who challenges Jason to a duel and later has her seal removed.",
 "- \"I am Tera Jun Casta... I will be the one to kill you\" (Book 9, Ch100 L19); fights comfortably with her abilities suppressed, in a practised, orthodox style (Book 9, Ch100 L49).\n- Her seal keeps her at silver rank; Jason removes it by working inside her soul (Book 9, Ch102 L54-67).\n- Her soul is branded and she was raised on lies (Book 10, Ch42 L7).",
 "Rigid, devout and furious at being freed.")
write("Allayeth","Allayeth","2","9","12","Books 9, 12 (chapter files)","Charist.md, ../06_Places/Yaresh.md",
 "One of Yaresh's two resident diamond-rank elves, the more reclusive of the pair.",
 "- Finds Schaat's corpse with Charist and sees a star phoenix (Book 9, Ch98 L4-5).\n- \"The more reclusive Lady Allayeth\" graces a VIP gathering; she raised the team Moon's Edge herself (Book 12, Ch16 L8).",
 "Cool, exact and difficult to read.")
write("Charist","Charist","2","9","12","Books 9, 12 (chapter files)","Allayeth.md, ../06_Places/Yaresh.md",
 "One of Yaresh's two resident diamond-rank elves, the more social of the pair.",
 "- Finds Schaat's corpse with Allayeth and demands to know \"what's going on here\" (Book 9, Ch98 L4-6).\n- \"Lord Charist was the more social of the two\" (Book 12, Ch16 L8); Allayeth and Charist discuss staying in the city because its people love Hana Shavar (Book 9, Ch104 L29).",
 "Sociable and watchful.")
write("Carlos_Quilido","Carlos Quilido","1","8","13","Books 8, 11, 13 (chapter files)","Jason_Asano.md, Arabelle_Remore.md, ../02_Cosmology_and_Powers/Gods_and_Churches.md",
 "A priest of the Healer who helps Jason restore his soul and later develops the Quilido Procedure.",
 "- \"The Healer Priest, Carlos Quilido, had helped Jason restore his damaged soul after it was besieged by the Builder's star seed\" (Book 8, Ch29 L44).\n- A humble man in simple clothes, though the world will not let a gold-ranker be too humble (Book 8, Ch41 L58).\n- Joins the Cardinas expedition with a new research team (Book 11, Ch67 L6; Ch68 L367).\n- The Quilido Procedure removes the taint of monster cores (Book 13, Ch1001 L9).",
 "Humble, scholarly and cautious about consequences.")
write("Liara_Rimaros","Liara Rimaros","1","7","13","Books 7, 8 (chapter files)","Soramir.md, Zara_Rimaros.md, ../06_Places/Rimaros.md",
 "A gold-rank member of the Rimaros royal house who screens adventurers for Builder cultists.",
 "- Works without rest as the city is overrun with adventurers to be filtered for potential cultists, and is a gold-ranker (Book 7, Ch17 L3).\n- \"Pelli and Liara Rimaros will be your contact points going forward\" for Jason (Book 7, Ch18 L95).\n- Her husband is Baseph and their three silver-rank children are Dara, Zareen and the youngest, Joseph, an administrative official (Book 8, Ch62 L28-32).",
 "Brisk, official and not unkind.")
write("Soramir","Soramir","2","7","7","Book 7 (chapter files)","Liara_Rimaros.md, Dawn.md, ../06_Places/Rimaros.md",
 "A palindromically named Rimaros royal.",
 "- Meets Jason in Book 7; palindromic first and last names \"were assigned in adulthood rather than at birth and denoted important members of a given family\" (Book 7, Ch18 L41-42).\n- Explains that the Hierophant is allowed to intervene in the world a single time (Book 7, Ch60 L27).",
 "Dignified and plain-spoken.")
write("Hana_Shavar","Hana Shavar","1","9","13","Books 9, 10 (chapter files)","Carlos_Quilido.md, ../02_Cosmology_and_Powers/Gods_and_Churches.md",
 "The elf High Priestess of the Healer for Yaresh.",
 "- \"The High Priestess of the Healer for the city-state of Yaresh\", who sends her priests into Bahadir's bunker rather than Jason's (Book 9, Ch80 L6-13).\n- Runs operations that use Jason's cloud palace as a base (Book 10, Ch3 L29).\n- Explains that the Church of Undeath acts rarely (Book 10, Ch78 L38).",
 "Warm, devout and plain about danger.")
write("Musin_Heath","Musin Heath","2","9","10","Books 9, 10 (chapter files); notes for Book 10","Hana_Shavar.md, ../06_Places/Yaresh.md",
 "The director of the Adventure Society's Yaresh branch.",
 "- \"Musin Heath, director of the Adventure Society's Yaresh branch\" (Book 10, Ch9 L38).\n- Announces a potential alliance with the messenger leader and shows his equanimity (Book 10, Ch10 L3); presents the messenger-delivered device with distrust (Book 10, Ch11 L4).\n- The notes make him an elf, gold-rank and a core-user (notes, Book 10).",
 "Careful, political and unflappable.")
write("Jamis_Fran_Muskar","Jamis Fran Muskar","3","10","12","Books 10, 12 (chapter files)","Boris_Ket_Lundi.md, ../02_Cosmology_and_Powers/Astral_Kings_and_Messengers.md",
 "An astral king whose avatar attends the Builder's observation scene and who berates defiant messengers.",
 "- His avatar is the only one whose wings are completely absorbed into his body (Book 10, Ch15 L6).\n- Says that when the task is complete \"the price is paid. Zithis Carrow Vayel will have fulfilled his debt to us\" (Book 10, Ch15 L9).\n- Snarls at defiant messengers that they directly defied the Council of Kings (Book 12, Ch33 L51-55).",
 "Indulgent, vain and sharp when crossed.")
write("Craig_Vermillion","Craig Vermillion","2","4","4","Book 4 (chapter files)","Boris_Ket_Lundi.md, ../05_Organisations/Earth_Powers.md",
 "A Cabal figure who explains the magical world to Jason.",
 "- Every aura in the room except Jason's and Ari's trembles at the name Vermillion (Book 4, Ch7 L49-50).\n- Explains the magical world's three dominant forces (Book 4, Ch10 L127) and says a new kind of magic appeared five centuries ago (Book 4, Ch11 L4).\n- Discusses Dawn's paintings with Jason (Book 4, Ch23 L31-39).\n- Is a vampire of seventy years' standing and the Cabal's front man in Sydney (notes, Book 4).",
 "Polished, patient and quietly dangerous.")
write("Mr_North","Mr North (Noreth)","3","5","13","Books 5, 13 (chapter files)","Gerling.md, ../05_Organisations/Earth_Powers.md",
 "The EOA Cardinal Mr North, who is the Network founder's former familiar Noreth.",
 "- The meeting room of the Four Cardinals of the EOA: Mr North and the new Mr East await Mrs West and Mrs South (Book 5, Ch8 L14-15).\n- Tells Jason \"I was a rune spider, originally\" (Book 5, Ch40 L79-83).\n- Jason's briefing names \"the founder's former familiar Noreth\" (Book 13, Ch1017 L39).",
 "Dry, old and amused; he treats everyone as a long game.")
write("Gerling","Gerling","2","5","13","Books 5, 6 (chapter files); notes for Books 5, 12, 13","Mr_North.md, Kaito_Asano.md",
 "A US Network gold-ranker who kills Kaito, Asya and Greg in Book 5.",
 "- Works with Chen and Guo in the transformation zones in Book 6 (Book 6, Ch6 L31; Ch7 L80).\n- Tells Mr Barbou he is not going to keep giving him a hard time (Book 6, Ch33 L28).\n- Proposes that Jason join the coalition against the vampires (Book 6, Ch42 L66).\n- The notes make him the killer of Kaito, Asya and Greg and later Elizabeth's blood slave (notes, Books 5, 12, 13).",
 "Cynical, practical and quick with a knife.")
write("Nigel_Thornton","Nigel Thornton","1","4","13","Books 4, 12, 13 (chapter files)","Itsuki_Tiwari.md, ../05_Organisations/Earth_Powers.md",
 "A Network tactical-team leader who becomes the first gold-ranker outside the US without cores.",
 "- Tells Jason his teams' methods are reaching their limits (Book 4, Ch41 L89-97).\n- \"Hadn't been the first person on Earth to hit gold rank, or even the first to do it without cores\"; his nine-person unit stayed together when the Network fractured (Book 12, Ch3 L3-8).\n- Still leads the nine-person unit in 2038 (Book 13, Ch1007 L23, L45).",
 "Steady, weary and loyal to his people.")
write("Melody_Jain","Melody Jain","2","6","9","Books 6, 7, 8, 9 (chapter files)","Sophie_Wexler.md, ../05_Organisations/Cults_and_Orders.md",
 "Sophie's mother, who faked her death twenty years ago and leads the Order of Redeeming Light in the Storm Kingdom.",
 "- Faked her death twenty years before Book 6, using a wall panel in Marta Fries's house in Kurdansk (Book 6, Ch47 L510-513).\n- \"The leader of the enclave\" of the Order with Sendira as second in command; she wants to lure her daughter to Rimaros (Book 7, Ch58 L38-46).\n- Leads the Order's local forces in the Sea of Storms (Book 8, Ch18 L3-6).\n- Sophie's mother Melody Jain is subjected to the mind-warping effects of the Order of Redemption (Book 9, Ch19 L3).",
 "Controlled and sincere; her faith has been engineered.")
write("Timos","Timos","1","2","3","Books 2, 3 (chapter files)","Zato.md, Thadwick_Mercer.md, ../05_Organisations/Cults_and_Orders.md",
 "A Builder cultist embedded in Greenstone for years.",
 "- \"Timos had been operating in Greenstone for years\" and regrets going along with Thadwick's self-recruitment (Book 2, Ch59 L87-90).\n- Facilitated most of the cult's insertions years earlier and ran operatives in compartmentalised groups (Book 3, Ch34 L10).\n- Kills Frank with a conjured spear (Book 2, Ch59 L106-110).",
 "Careful, patient and horrified by amateurs.")
write("Cressida_Vane","Cressida Vane","0","1","1","Book 1 (chapter files)","Landemere_Vane.md, ../05_Organisations/Cults_and_Orders.md",
 "The matriarch of the blood-cult family that holds Jason and his friends in Book 1.",
 "- \"I am Lady Cressida Vane\" (Book 1, Ch11 L80); Jason mocks her high-priestess name (Book 1, Ch11 L81-83).\n- Complains that astral beings were \"the death\" of her son, and that they are \"a nice, traditional blood cult family\" (Book 1, Ch9 L47-50).",
 "Haughty, weary of her family's ambitions.")
write("Landemere_Vane","Landemere Vane","1","1","7","Books 1, 2, 7 (chapter files)","Cressida_Vane.md, Jason_Asano.md",
 "The Vane heir whose failed summoning pulls Jason to Pallimustus.",
 "- His mother wonders what Landemere was trying to summon; Dougall says it was \"one of them entities from beyond the void\" (Book 1, Ch9 L47-50).\n- Clive explains in Book 7 that Landemere's summoning went wrong, possibly because he reached beyond his ability or a dimensional event interfered (Book 7, Ch55 L64-79).\n- Jason killed him; Clive regrets losing his notes (Book 2, Ch37 L67).",
 "Ambitious and out of his depth.")
